  "verse": "But your delusion also drives you to beget offspring in an uncontrolled wise and to increasingly push the world which is already overpopulated with human beings into an overpopulation disaster, out of which ever more immense problems emerge, and indeed besides the destruction of the nature and the climate also the thereout resulting natural catastrophes, pollution of air, water and soil, worldwide terrorism, wars, murder and other crimes, torture, epidemics, deficiency of water and famines, criminality, energy shortages…",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 159",
  "hinge": "The cause is the **choice to be told exactly what is coming and to spend the money elsewhere — the hottest month on record confirmed at 1.65°C above pre-industrial levels, an El Niño forecast to run to February 2027 with the strength of the century, fires in Indonesia scheduled by dryness to continue into November, a canal slowed by drought and rivers too thin to float a barge, an emissions standard withdrawn on the finding that the deaths are \"conjectural\", and the agency that would answer all of it cut back by a plan a court called illegal.** Verse 159 describes a chain in which the destruction of nature and climate is followed by precisely this catalogue — catastrophes, deficient water, famines, energy shortages — and it places the cause in the decisions of human beings rather than in any decree of fate. The measurements are not accusations; they are readings. The same law permits other causes, and the first of them is the cheapest: act on the forecast before the season, fund the response so that it exists when needed, and decline to withdraw the standards whose withdrawal the atmosphere does not notice and the household does. Whether the coming eighteen months are remembered as the season the warnings were used, or as the season they were filed and then paid for, is being decided in choices available now — and the effect will follow the cause that is set."
