  "verse": "To your human sense and your human view are also connected your earthly jurisdictions, but you must not expect that these are equivalent with the strength of the character and of all virtues of the Creation Universal Consciousness nor with the Creation-given laws and recommendations to which your earthly courts and their laws do not even get close; exactly the opposite is the case, because between your understanding of the fairness and of the creational fairness… there is generally in the true sense of the word a scandalous and shaking difference.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 372",
  "hinge": "The cause is the **choice to enforce the standard selectively and at the speed of politics — a former president sentenced to 25 years for 96 murders and 300 tortures while his own capital marches for acquittal, a former president before the ICC on video link, crimes against humanity found in one capital and machines barred from a crime scene in another, 8,000 people still waiting under collapsed buildings, and a superpower issuing visa bans in the name of discrimination against a minority in a country whose majority was dispossessed by law.** Verse 372 sets the limit with unusual directness: earthly jurisdictions \"do not even get close\" to creational fairness, and between human and creational understanding of fairness there is \"a scandalous and shaking difference\". That is not a counsel of despair — it is a description of the gap that must be closed deliberately, case by case, because no court closes it by existing. The finest of these instruments is also the cheapest: sequence the clearing of rubble so that evidence is preserved, admit the investigators, try the cases that are open, and apply the same measure to allies and adversaries. Whether this becomes the decade accountability became a tool in the hands of the powerful, or the decade it became a record that everyone had to read, is being decided in choices available now — and the effect will follow the cause that is set."
